WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.709 --> 00:00:14.689
stared at Mateo.

2
00:00:14.709 --> 00:00:16.910
"What kind of bad news?"

3
00:00:18.111 --> 00:00:19.251
"Let's sit down."

4
00:00:20.992 --> 00:00:22.893
Mateo led Ally to the dining room.

5
00:00:24.454 --> 00:00:25.054
Ally sat.

6
00:00:25.074 --> 00:00:29.356
"Okay, I'm sitting, tell me the bad news."

7
00:00:31.072 --> 00:00:35.435
"Eclipses are not visible from everywhere on Earth," Mateo said.

8
00:00:35.455 --> 00:00:39.237
"We won't be able to see the next one here in Sandville."

9
00:00:39.257 --> 00:00:40.858
"That's okay."

10
00:00:41.418 --> 00:00:42.038
Ally shrugged.

11
00:00:42.058 --> 00:00:44.240
"I'll just go where I can see it."

12
00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:47.402
"Here's the thing," Mateo said.

13
00:00:47.422 --> 00:00:49.823
"You'd have to go to Patagonia.

14
00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:52.985
It's very far away, in South America.

15
00:00:53.285 --> 00:00:54.846
You'd have to take a plane there."

16
00:00:54.866 --> 00:00:58.108
"I love flying," Ally said.

17
00:00:58.844 --> 00:01:01.906
"And it'll be fun to take an Earthlings' primitive jet."

18
00:01:01.926 --> 00:01:06.830
"Hmm. I guess that's possible," Mateo said.

19
00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:08.351
"Let's look at flights."

20
00:01:09.191 --> 00:01:13.555
While Mateo searched for plane tickets on his tablet, Ally sent Julius a text.

21
00:01:14.895 --> 00:01:15.116
Ally: Hi!

22
00:01:15.476 --> 00:01:16.637
Sorry about before.

23
00:01:17.197 --> 00:01:19.158
It looks like I might be taking a trip too!

24
00:01:19.219 --> 00:01:22.341
Julius: Cool!

25
00:01:22.601 --> 00:01:22.901
Where to?

26
00:01:22.961 --> 00:01:25.043
Ally: Patagonia.

27
00:01:25.503 --> 00:01:26.584
Have you ever heard of it?

28
00:01:28.408 --> 00:01:28.769
Julius: Sure.

29
00:01:28.889 --> 00:01:30.350
But why would you go there?

30
00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:32.392
Ally: Oh, no reason.

31
00:01:32.832 --> 00:01:36.716
I hear it's nice this time of "Uh-oh," Mateo said.

32
00:01:37.356 --> 00:01:37.977
Ally looked up.

33
00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:39.398
"What now?"

34
00:01:40.819 --> 00:01:41.660
Mateo sighed.

35
00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:47.906
"A round-trip ticket from Sandville to Patagonia costs two thousand dollars."

36
00:01:47.926 --> 00:01:50.488
"That's all right," Ally said.

37
00:01:50.508 --> 00:01:54.592
"I have some money saved up from work, and your dad won't let me pay rent.

38
00:01:55.184 --> 00:02:00.967
So, between my savings and the money from the contest, I—" She gasped.

39
00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:02.388
"What's wrong?"

40
00:02:02.728 --> 00:02:03.449
Mateo asked.

41
00:02:03.469 --> 00:02:05.530
"Silly me!

42
00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:07.751
I Ally could hardly get the words out.

43
00:02:08.632 --> 00:02:12.814
"I forgot that I spent all my money on the new phone and computer!"

44
00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:15.956
"Oh boy."

45
00:02:16.596 --> 00:02:19.457
Mateo shook his head, but then he perked up.

46
00:02:19.478 --> 00:02:22.079
"The computer was worth it though.

47
00:02:22.559 --> 00:02:23.740
Alpha is working now."

48
00:02:24.876 --> 00:02:25.436
"You're right.

49
00:02:25.897 --> 00:02:29.940
I wouldn't even know how to get my powers back without Alpha," Ally said.

50
00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:33.442
"I guess I'll just have to wait for the next eclipse.

51
00:02:33.922 --> 00:02:35.824
It has to be coming pretty soon, right?"

52
00:02:35.844 --> 00:02:37.845
"Let's see."

53
00:02:38.646 --> 00:02:40.147
Mateo tapped on his tablet.

54
00:02:41.748 --> 00:02:42.928
"I'm sorry, Ally.

55
00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:47.612
There won't be a solar eclipse visible here for eight years."

56
00:02:47.632 --> 00:02:53.656
"What?" Ally finished her text to Julius and got up to pace around the room.

57
00:02:55.532 --> 00:02:57.233
"I can't wait eight years!

58
00:02:57.634 --> 00:02:59.955
I have to find a way to get to Patagonia!"

59
00:03:01.716 --> 00:03:03.257
Mateo looked up from his tablet.

60
00:03:03.277 --> 00:03:05.219
"I have more bad news.

61
00:03:05.759 --> 00:03:08.581
You need a passport to travel to another country."

62
00:03:08.601 --> 00:03:10.762
"A pass what?"

63
00:03:11.283 --> 00:03:11.903
Ally asked.

64
00:03:12.704 --> 00:03:15.966
"Passport. It's a document that comes from the government.

65
00:03:16.486 --> 00:03:18.328
It takes eight weeks to get one.

66
00:03:19.088 --> 00:03:20.709
There's lots of red tape."

67
00:03:20.729 --> 00:03:23.411
"Then they should take the tape off!"

68
00:03:23.771 --> 00:03:24.412
Ally snapped.

69
00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:27.862
"Besides, I can't go anywhere near the government.

70
00:03:28.703 --> 00:03:31.985
Dr. Lloyd is working with them, looking for aliens!"

71
00:03:32.005 --> 00:03:34.967
"Let's ask Alpha.

72
00:03:35.467 --> 00:03:37.168
I bet she can find a solution."

73
00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:42.972
Mateo covered his mouth as he yawned.

74
00:03:44.513 --> 00:03:45.174
Ally sighed.

75
00:03:45.974 --> 00:03:48.656
"You've had a long day, Mateo.

76
00:03:49.617 --> 00:03:50.317
Go to sleep.

77
00:03:50.718 --> 00:03:52.099
I'll get Alpha to work on it.

78
00:03:52.719 --> 00:03:53.880
She'll find the answer."

79
00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:56.780
Ally tried to sound hopeful.

80
00:03:57.161 --> 00:03:59.361
But inside all she felt was worry.

81
00:03:59.381 --> 00:04:04.423
"If Alpha can't help me, I'll have to get used to being a human!"

82
00:04:04.823 --> 00:04:05.283
she thought.

83
00:04:08.524 --> 00:04:11.164
The next morning at work, Ally was distracted.

84
00:04:14.285 --> 00:04:17.346
Alpha had promised to have an answer for Ally by the end of the day.

85
00:04:17.366 --> 00:04:21.927
"What if Alpha can't figure out how I can get to Patagonia?"

86
00:04:22.287 --> 00:04:25.024
she thought as she refilled saltshakers.

87
00:04:25.044 --> 00:04:27.685
"I can't stay on Earth for eight more years!"

88
00:04:28.585 --> 00:04:30.126
Soon Phil and Tina came in.

89
00:04:34.527 --> 00:04:38.428
coffees and two of my regular breakfast sandwiches to go," Phil said.

90
00:04:39.108 --> 00:04:40.368
Tina looked very proud.

91
00:04:40.388 --> 00:04:45.130
"Phil's going to give me my own set of keys to the museum today."

92
00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:47.810
"Huh. That's nice for you."

93
00:04:49.871 --> 00:04:50.471
Ally sighed.

94
00:04:50.491 --> 00:04:52.332
"You okay, Ally?"

95
00:04:52.752 --> 00:04:53.392
Phil asked.

96
00:04:54.272 --> 00:04:56.013
"You're not your usual sunny self."

97
00:04:57.013 --> 00:04:59.314
"Of course, I'm myself," Ally said.

98
00:04:59.334 --> 00:05:01.075
"Who else would I be?"

99
00:05:01.095 --> 00:05:04.376
Tina laughed.

100
00:05:05.117 --> 00:05:06.737
"You're funny, Ally!

101
00:05:06.757 --> 00:05:12.320
Oh, I was wondering how that fancy new computer of yours is working."

102
00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:14.861
"Yes," Ally said.

103
00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:18.082
"Why do you keep—" "Ally!

104
00:05:18.222 --> 00:05:19.283
Your order is up!"

105
00:05:19.663 --> 00:05:20.403
Melanie called.

106
00:05:20.423 --> 00:05:25.917
"Coming!" "Why does Tina keep asking me about the computer?"

107
00:05:26.317 --> 00:05:28.057
Ally thought as she picked up the order.

108
00:05:28.077 --> 00:05:32.539
"If I had my mind-reading powers, I could find out."

109
00:05:33.839 --> 00:05:36.800
Melanie watched Ally balance five dishes in her arms.

110
00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:39.561
"You sure you can handle all that at once?"

111
00:05:39.581 --> 00:05:42.061
"Of course I can!"

112
00:05:42.441 --> 00:05:43.181
Ally replied.

113
00:05:45.922 --> 00:05:49.563
But as she hurried to deliver the meals, she tripped over a customer's foot.

114
00:05:49.583 --> 00:05:51.964
"Great Galorpian goats!"

115
00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:53.201
Ally cried.

116
00:05:53.942 --> 00:05:58.907
The three plates of pancakes and two bowls of oatmeal flew up in the air before crashing down

117
00:05:58.967 --> 00:05:59.468
on the floor.
